# ProblemProof — configuration
#
# ONE file for the whole project. Copy to `.env` in this same directory and
# edit; `.env` is gitignored, this template is not.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Both halves read it:
#   backend   loads it at startup (backend/problemproof/env.py)
#   frontend  Vite reads it via `envDir: ".."` in frontend/vite.config.ts
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS ARE SAFE IN HERE, WITH ONE RULE.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed `VITE_` to the browser bundle. Anything
# without that prefix stays server-side and is never shipped to the client.
#
# So: never prefix a secret with VITE_. If you do, it lands in the JavaScript
# bundle and anyone with devtools can read it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# === Backend ===============================================================

# Where sessions and candidate baselines are stored.
# Default: backend/data
# PP_DATA_ROOT=/srv/problemproof/data

# Bind address for `python main.py`.
# PP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PP_PORT=8000

# Set to anything to enable uvicorn auto-reload in development.
# PP_RELOAD=1

# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API.
# Default: http://localhost:5173 (the Vite dev server)
# PP_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# Override the bundled MediaPipe Face Landmarker model.
# PP_FACE_LANDMARKER_MODEL=/path/to/face_landmarker.task


# === AI tooling =============================================================
#
# There is no in-portal AI assistant during a session. Participants use
# whatever AI tools and websites they like, in their own browser; that use is
# reconstructed afterwards from OS-level capture and validated against
# hand-annotated screen recordings. See docs/SYSTEM.md §4.3. Nothing to
# configure for that.
#
# The personalisation layer (CV -> skill graph, backend/problemproof/profile/)
# has two OPTIONAL, OFF-BY-DEFAULT extraction tiers below the always-on
# dictionary. Neither needs configuring to use the product; both need an
# explicit sentinel to turn on, never a truthy value, so a stray "1" inherited
# from a copied .env cannot enable either by accident.

# ESCO-grounded skill matching (problemproof/profile/esco.py). Local sentence-
# transformer embeddings against a bundled public taxonomy -- no network call
# at match time beyond a one-time model download, no CV content sent anywhere.
# Needs `pip install sentence-transformers` (see backend/requirements.txt).
# PP_ESCO_SKILL_MATCHING=on

# LLM-assisted skill cleanup (problemproof/profile/llm_cleanup.py), via NVIDIA
# NIM. The ONE tier that leaves the machine — sends only short, already-
# isolated skill phrases the dictionary and ESCO both missed (never CV prose,
# a name, an employer, or a date) to correct spelling/formatting, with every
# proposal checked against the original before being shown. Confirmed with the
# user before being built; see problemproof/profile/llm_cleanup.py's module
# docstring for the guardrails.
# PP_NIM_SKILL_CLEANUP=on
# PP_NIM_API_KEY=
# PP_NIM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# PP_NIM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct


# === Mode ==================================================================
#
# Whether this process is a real deployment or a developer's machine.
#
#   deployment   (default) Everything is strict. Calibration must pass before
#                a session can start, and there is no way around it.
#
#   development  Mounts POST /api/dev/exam-ticket, which mints an exam ticket
#                with NO calibration run behind it, so the exam flow can be
#                worked on from a machine where calibration cannot pass — a
#                poor webcam, bad light, a room that is not quiet.
#
# Development mode does NOT make a bad calibration pass. It skips calibration
# and says so. When calibration runs, it runs strict in both modes: a baseline
# fitted from dark, off-centre frames is a transform that is *wrong* rather
# than missing, and every later session signal is scored in it.
#
# What it costs, plainly. A session started this way has no verified person, no
# baseline profile, and its webcam signals fall back to default blink
# thresholds. Its manifest records `calibration: bypassed_development`, and
# `feature_assembly.session_readiness` excludes it from the analysis corpus.
# It is good for checking the pipeline runs end to end. It is not research
# data, and it must never be counted alongside real sessions.
#
# Default: deployment. Absent, empty, or misspelled all mean deployment —
# `dev`, `1` and `true` do NOT enable it. The exact lowercase word is the only
# spelling that opens the door, so that `grep -r PP_MODE=development` finds
# every place it could be on.
# PP_MODE=development

# === Frontend ==============================================================
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables reach the browser. Keep it that way.

# Backend base URL used by every client in frontend/src/lib.
# Default: http://localhost:8000
# VITE_PP_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
